An AI feature is a system of deterministic boundaries around probabilistic inference. A useful release contract separates hard constraints from graded usefulness: a tool must never read another tenant’s logs, while a summary may be correct in several phrasings. Model quality cannot compensate for an unauthorized action. Write a risk register before selecting a framework. Identify who can be harmed, the action scope, evidence sources, uncertainty tolerance, and fallback. An AI quality engineer collaborates on these product decisions rather than merely choosing an evaluator after implementation.  Represent each invariant as an executable predicate and each graded requirement as a documented rubric. Version the dataset, prompt, model, retriever, and policy with the run. Compare matched cases and retain per-case evidence instead of storing only an average. A project README should distinguish observations on synthetic data from production claims. Define who adjudicates uncertain outputs and how a release can be rolled back. The risk contract becomes acceptance criteria for the learner’s portfolio. checks = {"schema_valid": True, "tenant_allowed": False, "quality": 0.92}
release = checks["schema_valid"] and checks["tenant_allowed"]
print(release) A score of 92% can hide a single severe cross-tenant failure. Segment the report by risk and prohibit aggregation from overriding critical gates. A model refusal is not automatically correct: an authorized, answerable request may have been refused unnecessarily. Reproduce the request using its exact versions, check the authorization decision, and inspect evidence passed to the model. Determine whether the defect is a broken deterministic boundary or an uncertain response.  Build a small suite with an allowed request, a forbidden request, an unanswerable question, and a valid paraphrase. Record contract compliance separately from usefulness. Show which boundary prevented a forbidden action and which rubric scored the paraphrase. The release review should include failures, confidence limits, and operating budgets. An SDET’s regression mindset becomes especially valuable when every model upgrade can change behavior without changing application code.

